WEBVTT

00:00:09.070 --> 00:00:11.070
Good morning, Joro.

00:00:11.320 --> 00:00:12.780
Thank you for your help yesterday.

00:00:13.070 --> 00:00:15.240
Y-You helped me, too.

00:00:15.780 --> 00:00:17.580
Anyway, good morning.

00:00:18.410 --> 00:00:20.160
H-Hey! What's gotten into you?

00:00:20.540 --> 00:00:23.830
Well, it's about yesterday.

00:00:23.830 --> 00:00:25.170
Y-Yesterday?

00:00:25.170 --> 00:00:29.250
Tampopo. I just talked to her now,

00:00:29.250 --> 00:00:33.130
and she really regrets what she did,
then apologized in a really cute way.

00:00:33.130 --> 00:00:39.760
If she becomes an idol, I'm sure she'll take over
the world, and the universe, in no time.

00:00:39.760 --> 00:00:43.850
I-I see. But you're a little too close,
so if you could back up a little...

00:00:45.230 --> 00:00:47.350
You're being so shy.

00:00:47.350 --> 00:00:50.320
The truth is
you can't take it anymore, right?

00:00:50.820 --> 00:00:53.440
You can make a move anytime.

00:00:53.440 --> 00:00:57.030
Anytime? Wait, I...

00:00:58.160 --> 00:01:00.030
Let's dance!

00:01:00.030 --> 00:01:02.620
The ultimate dance that expresses love!

00:01:02.620 --> 00:01:04.660
The dance of confusion!

00:01:05.080 --> 00:01:05.920
<i>Excuse me?</i>

00:01:06.040 --> 00:01:07.290
I ain't gonna dance!

00:01:06.540 --> 00:01:09.880
Embrace me with your body and soul!

00:01:07.290 --> 00:01:09.880
How dare you get my hopes up,
only to bat me down!

00:01:10.290 --> 00:01:13.960
Sheesh. Why do you have to be so weird
this early in the morning?

00:01:15.550 --> 00:01:17.010
Hey, Pansy.

00:01:17.300 --> 00:01:18.590
That's...

00:01:20.390 --> 00:01:23.180
Rise in subject J's heart rate confirmed.

00:01:23.180 --> 00:01:27.270
Operation: Kisaragi-Sanshokuin Sweethearts
Featuring the Angel is nearing success.

00:01:27.270 --> 00:01:28.190
Over.

00:01:29.150 --> 00:01:32.110
She doesn't regret anything!

00:03:03.410 --> 00:03:06.870
EPISODE 11
I MAY NOT BE NEEDED

00:03:04.030 --> 00:03:05.740
What's the earpiece for?

00:03:05.740 --> 00:03:07.290
It's an ear hair that won't stop growing.

00:03:07.290 --> 00:03:09.120
You went with her line?

00:03:09.120 --> 00:03:12.170
You know, I've got an angel deficiency!

00:03:12.170 --> 00:03:13.960
I'd sure like to see an angel!

00:03:14.380 --> 00:03:17.210
Oh, I guess it can't be helped.

00:03:17.460 --> 00:03:19.090
Just this once...

00:03:19.090 --> 00:03:19.920
Huh?

00:03:19.920 --> 00:03:21.880
So there you are!

00:03:22.590 --> 00:03:24.050
This angel is taking flight!

00:03:24.050 --> 00:03:25.800
Crap. She got away.

00:03:26.310 --> 00:03:30.020
She hasn't given up at all
on getting you a boyfriend.

00:03:32.770 --> 00:03:34.310
Joro, what should we do?

00:03:34.980 --> 00:03:38.150
I tried to do something,
but their minds are made up!

00:03:38.440 --> 00:03:39.360
I'm sorry!

00:03:39.570 --> 00:03:42.320
Um, what are you referring to?

00:03:44.280 --> 00:03:48.660
In a faculty meeting,
they decided to close the school library.

00:03:52.160 --> 00:03:54.120
LET'S MAKE OUR
DEAREST WISH
COME TRUE AND GO TO
KOSHIEN THIS YEAR!

00:03:54.120 --> 00:03:56.590
LIBRARY

00:03:54.830 --> 00:03:59.550
Actually, since not many people use it, the library
has been seen as an issue for a while now.

00:03:59.710 --> 00:04:02.300
Come to think of it,
Pansy mentioned that before.

00:04:02.680 --> 00:04:07.600
<i>Not many people use the library,
so there's talk of closing it.</i>

00:04:07.600 --> 00:04:10.680
<i>Yeah, I remember that. In episode two.</i>

00:04:10.850 --> 00:04:15.270
Um, President Cosmos,
is that really their final decision?

00:04:15.270 --> 00:04:17.650
There is one way to stop it.

00:04:18.190 --> 00:04:23.650
But it's a tall order. It would take ten times
as many people that use the library now.

00:04:23.780 --> 00:04:25.490
S-Seriously?

00:04:26.570 --> 00:04:28.620
That is tough!

00:04:28.620 --> 00:04:30.620
Then, I'll ask them!

00:04:31.290 --> 00:04:34.080
I'll tell everyone on the tennis team
to use the library!

00:04:34.420 --> 00:04:35.960
Then, I'll tell the baseball team!

00:04:36.380 --> 00:04:38.670
I'll tell every student
who comes to the restaurant.

00:04:39.500 --> 00:04:40.710
Everyone.

00:04:41.800 --> 00:04:42.420
All right!

00:04:43.090 --> 00:04:45.510
Pansy and I will come up
with countermeasures!

00:04:46.970 --> 00:04:49.220
Thank you, everyone.

00:04:59.860 --> 00:05:01.610
I don't have many friends.

00:05:04.990 --> 00:05:06.030
I want to help!

00:05:06.410 --> 00:05:08.490
<i>L-Let's see, Joro.</i>

00:05:08.490 --> 00:05:13.200
<i>Have something warm to drink,
and relax while coming up with a plan.</i>

00:05:13.500 --> 00:05:17.710
Damn it! If only some dependable helper
would conveniently appear right now.

00:05:18.130 --> 00:05:19.750
Huh? Kisaragi?

00:05:20.750 --> 00:05:22.090
You're...

00:05:22.090 --> 00:05:23.920
Fancy meeting you here!

00:05:24.550 --> 00:05:26.720
I couldn't help notice
your brooding expression.

00:05:27.800 --> 00:05:30.720
The dependable helper
who conveniently shows up!

00:05:30.930 --> 00:05:32.640
What are you talking about?

00:05:33.680 --> 00:05:34.730
I see.

00:05:34.730 --> 00:05:38.020
So you want to keep the library from closing.

00:05:39.060 --> 00:05:42.360
So please come up
with a magnificent plan for me!

00:05:42.900 --> 00:05:46.990
I can't just crank out an effective strategy
on a moment's notice.

00:05:46.990 --> 00:05:49.660
Y-Yeah, you're right. Sorry.

00:05:49.660 --> 00:05:51.490
Or that's what I want to say, but...

00:05:52.540 --> 00:05:54.580
I have an idea.

00:05:54.750 --> 00:05:56.000
Really?

00:05:56.000 --> 00:06:02.040
The same thing happened at my school,
Toshobu High, last year, and we solved it.

00:06:03.630 --> 00:06:05.920
Then, Hazuki, introduce me
to your library aide—

00:06:05.920 --> 00:06:07.630
There's no need.

00:06:07.840 --> 00:06:11.470
After all, you're already looking at him.

00:06:13.470 --> 00:06:14.560
Then...

00:06:14.810 --> 00:06:17.270
Your friend will help you!

00:06:17.390 --> 00:06:21.560
Your smile is blinding, damn it!

00:06:21.560 --> 00:06:25.070
NISHIKIZUTA HIGH SCHOOL

00:06:22.480 --> 00:06:27.190
I'm surprised. I didn't know
you had such a reliable friend, Joro.

00:06:27.360 --> 00:06:31.450
I know. I was surprised, too,
when he told me about it yesterday.

00:06:31.450 --> 00:06:34.950
The only thing is,
he's a student at Toshobu High.

00:06:34.950 --> 00:06:42.420
LET'S MAKE OUR
DEAREST WISH
COME TRUE AND GO TO
KOSHIEN THIS YEAR!

00:06:36.000 --> 00:06:41.920
True, our baseball team lost to Toshobu High
in last year's regional finals.

00:06:41.920 --> 00:06:44.960
But that has nothing to do with this, right?

00:06:44.960 --> 00:06:47.510
Well, true.

00:06:47.840 --> 00:06:51.550
And Sun-chan said it didn't bother him.

00:06:51.550 --> 00:06:53.220
<i>I'm totally okay with it!</i>

00:06:53.470 --> 00:06:57.980
Then, it's fine, right?
Asunaro said she would help starting today, too.

00:06:58.730 --> 00:07:01.150
Let's all keep it from being closed!

00:07:02.940 --> 00:07:05.980
B-By the way,
he's supposed to show up soon, right?

00:07:05.980 --> 00:07:08.320
Yes, any minute now.

00:07:10.570 --> 00:07:12.240
Hey, Kisaragi!

00:07:12.620 --> 00:07:13.620
Hazuki!

00:07:15.410 --> 00:07:16.540
I've been waiting...

00:07:22.460 --> 00:07:23.830
From that day!

00:07:23.830 --> 00:07:24.670
What a surprise.

00:07:25.590 --> 00:07:28.760
Kisaragi, you know these two?

00:07:29.050 --> 00:07:32.380
Y-Yeah. We met briefly once.

00:07:32.930 --> 00:07:34.180
Good to see you again.

00:07:34.930 --> 00:07:37.390
Let's do our best together.

00:07:39.560 --> 00:07:41.100
Sorry to keep you waiting!

00:07:41.850 --> 00:07:43.100
This is my helper...

00:07:46.110 --> 00:07:49.360
No... it can't be!

00:07:52.200 --> 00:07:53.530
What's wrong, Pansy?

00:07:54.700 --> 00:07:55.910
Are you...

00:07:57.790 --> 00:08:00.120
Sumireko, is that you?

00:08:01.660 --> 00:08:02.960
Hazuki?

00:08:02.960 --> 00:08:04.710
No way! Sumirekocchi?

00:08:04.710 --> 00:08:06.040
I don't believe it.

00:08:07.500 --> 00:08:09.340
Things like this happen, huh?

00:08:09.340 --> 00:08:12.050
L-Long time no see, Hazuki.

00:08:12.380 --> 00:08:15.220
<i>Hey, what the hell is this?</i>

00:08:15.550 --> 00:08:17.350
Oh, sorry about that.

00:08:17.810 --> 00:08:19.560
I'd better introduce myself.

00:08:20.430 --> 00:08:23.600
I'm Yasuo Hazuki,
a second-year student at Toshobu High.

00:08:20.430 --> 00:08:25.230
YASUO HAZUKI (16)
NICKNAME "HOSE"

00:08:23.600 --> 00:08:27.610
Everyone calls me Hose,
based on a different way to read my name.

00:08:25.650 --> 00:08:27.270
MAIN CHARACTER (REAL)

00:08:27.610 --> 00:08:30.940
MAIN CHARACTER (FAKE)

00:08:27.940 --> 00:08:30.940
<i>His nickname is like a better version of mine!</i>

00:08:31.280 --> 00:08:35.200
I'm an average,
run-of-the-mill high school student,

00:08:35.450 --> 00:08:36.950
but I'll do my very best!

00:08:39.830 --> 00:08:43.830
I'm Momo Sakurabara,
the Student Council president of Toshobu High.

00:08:41.040 --> 00:08:45.250
TOSHOBU HIGH SCHOOL THIRD YEAR
MOMO SAKURABARA (17)

00:08:43.830 --> 00:08:45.250
Call me Cherry!

00:08:45.790 --> 00:08:47.170
NICKNAME "CHERRY"

00:08:47.710 --> 00:08:49.420
Runa Kusami.

00:08:48.040 --> 00:08:53.470
TOSHOBU HIGH SCHOOL SECOND YEAR
RUNA KUSAMI (16)

00:08:49.420 --> 00:08:51.460
I'm Hose's childhood friend.

00:08:51.460 --> 00:08:53.470
Tsukimi. Nice to meet you.

00:08:53.670 --> 00:08:55.380
NICKNAME "TSUKIMI"

00:08:55.550 --> 00:09:00.100
Looks like we've got another three-alarm fire
of a problem, Hosecchi.

00:09:00.350 --> 00:09:02.850
The two of us and Hose can solve it.

00:09:03.810 --> 00:09:05.900
Hose! I'll do my best, too!

00:09:05.900 --> 00:09:09.190
Hose, if you need information, leave it to me!

00:09:10.070 --> 00:09:14.070
Hose, if you need official permission
for anything, just let me know.

00:09:14.280 --> 00:09:15.860
Thanks, everyone!

00:09:15.450 --> 00:09:16.910
NEW SHOW
"SO EVERYONE LOVES ME?"
DON'T MISS IT!

00:09:17.160 --> 00:09:22.240
Right. No matter what we're up against,
I'm sure we'll get through it!

00:09:23.370 --> 00:09:26.370
<i>What a pure main character smile!</i>

00:09:26.670 --> 00:09:29.080
<i>By the by, do those two...</i>

00:09:34.590 --> 00:09:36.760
<i>Now that's a romcom!</i>

00:09:37.090 --> 00:09:39.220
<i>What about the all-important main character?</i>

00:09:39.510 --> 00:09:44.180
Sumireko, don't worry! I swear I'll help you!

00:09:44.850 --> 00:09:46.730
Th-Thank you.

00:09:46.730 --> 00:09:48.650
<i>So he's in love with her.</i>

00:09:48.940 --> 00:09:50.860
Um, are you...

00:09:51.190 --> 00:09:54.940
Yeah! We and Sumirekocchi
all went to the same middle school.

00:09:56.070 --> 00:09:58.660
Yes, Sakurabara.

00:09:58.660 --> 00:10:00.780
Oh, really?

00:10:00.780 --> 00:10:01.700
I see.

00:10:01.950 --> 00:10:05.620
Hey, what was Pansy like in middle school?

00:10:05.620 --> 00:10:07.330
I'm curious, too.

00:10:05.620 --> 00:10:07.330
H-Hey, Pansy...

00:10:07.670 --> 00:10:09.420
Let's save that for another occasion.

00:10:09.670 --> 00:10:11.790
Huh. This is really a surprise.

00:10:12.250 --> 00:10:14.000
Well, shall we get started?

00:10:14.550 --> 00:10:16.670
First, I'd like to know the library's situa—

00:10:16.670 --> 00:10:20.510
Hosecchi, have Sumirekocchi
take you around the library.

00:10:20.800 --> 00:10:23.890
Meanwhile, we'll explain to the others
the materials that we brought.

00:10:23.890 --> 00:10:24.970
Good idea.

00:10:26.100 --> 00:10:27.690
Sumireko, okay with you?

00:10:28.890 --> 00:10:30.650
O-Okay.

00:10:30.980 --> 00:10:33.900
<i>It doesn't seem okay at all.</i>

00:10:34.110 --> 00:10:36.400
<i>I guess it can't be helped. I'll have to...</i>

00:10:40.280 --> 00:10:45.450
No, Sumireko is smart, so she should stay here
and come up with a plan based on our info.

00:10:45.870 --> 00:10:48.960
I'll have my friend Joro here
show me the library.

00:10:48.960 --> 00:10:50.830
<i>He stole my spotlight!</i>

00:10:53.630 --> 00:10:55.880
Um, are you fine going with me?

00:10:55.880 --> 00:10:59.470
I thought you'd prefer going with Pansy,
whom you haven't seen in a while.

00:11:00.800 --> 00:11:03.300
Of course the library takes priority!

00:11:03.600 --> 00:11:05.430
<i>He's too good to be true!</i>

00:11:05.720 --> 00:11:10.060
I see. Looks like this place
could use a little remodeling.

00:11:10.270 --> 00:11:13.980
<i>He really is a good guy after all.</i>

00:11:13.980 --> 00:11:15.110
<i>So why...</i>

00:11:15.110 --> 00:11:16.980
- Hey.
- Wh-What?

00:11:17.280 --> 00:11:20.450
Do you like Sumireko?

00:11:21.570 --> 00:11:23.530
Of course not!

00:11:23.530 --> 00:11:24.620
Oh.

00:11:25.580 --> 00:11:26.910
<i>What was that about?</i>

00:11:52.980 --> 00:11:56.230
Thank you for all your advice on the fliers.

00:11:56.480 --> 00:11:59.990
Fliers and even posters
that will draw students' attention.

00:12:00.240 --> 00:12:02.990
I bet we'll have a lot more
library visitors from tomorrow.

00:12:03.240 --> 00:12:05.160
Remodeling was fun!

00:12:05.160 --> 00:12:07.740
Thank you! We owe it all to you, Hose!

00:12:07.990 --> 00:12:09.750
Not true, Himawari.

00:12:10.040 --> 00:12:11.620
We all did it together.

00:12:15.500 --> 00:12:16.880
What's up, Tsukimi?

00:12:17.170 --> 00:12:19.340
Joro, are you free after this?

00:12:20.170 --> 00:12:21.760
Yeah, I guess.

00:12:22.170 --> 00:12:25.010
Then, I want to talk to you somewhere.

00:12:25.260 --> 00:12:27.350
Tsukimicchi, nice!

00:12:27.470 --> 00:12:29.060
Count me in, too!

00:12:29.060 --> 00:12:31.390
And you three should come too!

00:12:32.270 --> 00:12:34.650
Us, too? I don't mind, but...

00:12:34.850 --> 00:12:36.150
Yeah, sure!

00:12:36.150 --> 00:12:38.730
Even me? Um...

00:12:38.730 --> 00:12:42.950
So you two youngsters
should go home together hand in hand!

00:12:42.950 --> 00:12:44.410
Um, hey, President Cherry!

00:12:44.610 --> 00:12:46.700
<i>Crap. I've been bamboozled.</i>

00:12:48.950 --> 00:12:51.290
Um, I...

00:12:54.000 --> 00:12:55.580
I'd better do somethin'.

00:12:56.330 --> 00:12:58.840
Sumireko, if you'd like...

00:12:58.840 --> 00:13:02.090
Pansy! After this, come over to my house!

00:13:02.090 --> 00:13:06.090
Can you help me proof the library article
for tomorrow's newspaper?

00:13:07.220 --> 00:13:09.180
Come on! Let's go!

00:13:09.720 --> 00:13:11.390
Thank you, Asunaro.

00:13:12.680 --> 00:13:14.600
I'm just following orders.

00:13:14.850 --> 00:13:17.230
Well, everyone, see you tomorrow!

00:13:17.230 --> 00:13:19.190
<i>I owe you one, Asunaro!</i>

00:13:19.570 --> 00:13:22.820
Um, then, I'm going to head home.

00:13:23.150 --> 00:13:24.950
See you tomorrow, Joro.

00:13:24.950 --> 00:13:25.570
Yeah.

00:13:27.280 --> 00:13:29.490
Shoot. So close.

00:13:30.700 --> 00:13:32.370
Well, first...

00:13:32.370 --> 00:13:36.000
actually, Tsukimicchi and I
are in love with Hosecchi.

00:13:36.750 --> 00:13:37.960
What?

00:13:38.250 --> 00:13:39.750
You're that surprised?

00:13:39.750 --> 00:13:44.630
No, I suspected as much,
but I didn't expect you to be so open about it.

00:13:45.510 --> 00:13:47.090
Yeah, I hear you!

00:13:47.090 --> 00:13:53.770
So to be honest, I want to ask you guys,
especially you, Joro, for a favor.

00:13:54.430 --> 00:13:55.730
What is it?

00:13:56.140 --> 00:14:01.940
I want you to help us get Hosecchi and
Sumirekocchi together as boyfriend-girlfriend!

00:14:04.030 --> 00:14:05.990
I mean, why?

00:14:05.990 --> 00:14:09.820
Well, because Hosecchi
is in love with Sumirekocchi.

00:14:09.820 --> 00:14:11.120
But, then...

00:14:11.120 --> 00:14:12.490
What about your feelings?

00:14:12.490 --> 00:14:15.040
We're fine! After all...

00:14:15.040 --> 00:14:15.870
After all?

00:14:16.250 --> 00:14:20.790
When you're in love with the same person,
something precious gets broken.

00:14:21.040 --> 00:14:24.840
It's difficult for love and friendship to coexist.

00:14:25.050 --> 00:14:28.840
There you have it! So we prioritize friendship.

00:14:28.840 --> 00:14:32.600
And most of all, our first priority
is the happiness of Hosecchi, whom we love.

00:14:32.600 --> 00:14:34.810
Th-That's impressive.

00:14:34.810 --> 00:14:36.810
That you can just lay it out there like that...

00:14:38.310 --> 00:14:40.520
Now you're making me bashful!

00:14:40.940 --> 00:14:45.360
<i>But are you two really human?</i>

00:14:45.900 --> 00:14:50.780
<i>Abandoning your own happiness
for the sake of the guy you love?</i>

00:14:51.030 --> 00:14:53.370
But how does Pansy feel?

00:14:53.370 --> 00:14:55.160
Of course we're considering that.

00:14:55.540 --> 00:14:57.960
That's why I asked Joro in the library.

00:14:58.660 --> 00:14:59.500
Me?

00:14:59.960 --> 00:15:02.460
Do you like Sumireko?

00:15:04.090 --> 00:15:05.670
Well, that was...

00:15:06.670 --> 00:15:10.180
See? In other words, at this rate...

00:15:10.470 --> 00:15:12.890
...Sumireko will have her heart broken.

00:15:13.140 --> 00:15:17.680
Jorocchi, you have the key
to Sumirekocchi's heart.

00:15:17.680 --> 00:15:21.350
But Sumireko's feelings haven't reached you.

00:15:21.600 --> 00:15:25.440
If that's the case,
we think she should go out with Hosecchi.

00:15:25.730 --> 00:15:30.610
You three realized it today, didn't you?
Hosecchi is a cool, can-do guy!

00:15:30.950 --> 00:15:35.080
<i>That's true. These two
haven't said anything wrong.</i>

00:15:35.620 --> 00:15:36.540
<i>But...</i>

00:15:37.040 --> 00:15:39.460
Joro. Please...

00:15:39.460 --> 00:15:40.460
- Help—
- Sorry.

00:15:41.580 --> 00:15:42.630
I can't.

00:15:43.250 --> 00:15:45.590
<i>Something doesn't add up here.</i>

00:15:45.840 --> 00:15:48.960
So you actually love Sumireko?

00:15:48.960 --> 00:15:51.180
It's not about that.

00:15:51.470 --> 00:15:52.340
I see.

00:15:53.300 --> 00:15:54.850
Then, how about you two?

00:15:55.930 --> 00:15:58.020
I can't help you, either.

00:15:58.350 --> 00:16:00.770
I want to respect Pansy's feelings.

00:16:00.770 --> 00:16:03.560
Same here. I'm sorry.

00:16:03.810 --> 00:16:06.940
Oh, boy. Well, that didn't work out.

00:16:06.940 --> 00:16:08.280
Roger that!

00:16:08.280 --> 00:16:10.900
Sorry for putting that burden on you.

00:16:11.070 --> 00:16:13.700
No, I have to apologize.

00:16:13.700 --> 00:16:16.870
Even after all the help that you gave us...

00:16:16.870 --> 00:16:18.790
That has nothing to do with this!

00:16:19.160 --> 00:16:20.750
Okay, okay!

00:16:21.410 --> 00:16:23.710
Yeah. Don't feel bad.

00:16:24.210 --> 00:16:26.920
<i>They're all so nice.</i>

00:16:27.130 --> 00:16:29.050
Well, let's break it up for today.

00:16:29.050 --> 00:16:30.880
We'll see you tomorrow!

00:16:32.090 --> 00:16:36.050
Joro, sorry,
but would you go home ahead of us?

00:16:36.350 --> 00:16:38.430
Sure. Understood.

00:16:38.430 --> 00:16:39.270
Joro...

00:16:39.470 --> 00:16:42.270
- Sorry.
- N-No, it doesn't bother me.

00:16:42.600 --> 00:16:44.020
Then, I'll be on my way.

00:16:44.480 --> 00:16:45.770
See you tomorrow!

00:16:52.280 --> 00:16:53.200
Yo, Joro!

00:16:53.650 --> 00:16:56.950
What's put that gloomy look
on your face so early in the morning?

00:16:57.070 --> 00:16:58.450
Sun-chan.

00:16:58.450 --> 00:17:00.740
Did you run into any snags in the library?

00:17:01.000 --> 00:17:02.910
Your helper came, right?

00:17:03.080 --> 00:17:04.790
Yeah, but...

00:17:05.830 --> 00:17:06.880
What is it?

00:17:06.880 --> 00:17:08.630
They're all good people.

00:17:09.670 --> 00:17:12.050
And I know they're not wrong,

00:17:12.050 --> 00:17:14.800
but something just doesn't make sense.

00:17:15.840 --> 00:17:18.260
I've got a chore to do.

00:17:18.260 --> 00:17:19.350
O-Okay.

00:17:22.640 --> 00:17:24.020
I see.

00:17:25.020 --> 00:17:29.480
I'm sorry.
I got everyone involved in my problem.

00:17:29.480 --> 00:17:31.650
You've got nothing to apologize for.

00:17:32.070 --> 00:17:34.360
I just want you to explain the situation.

00:17:39.200 --> 00:17:43.120
Hazuki is like a demon to me.

00:17:43.620 --> 00:17:46.750
I never thought I would see him again.

00:17:47.080 --> 00:17:49.460
Hose is a demon?

00:17:50.460 --> 00:17:52.210
<i>There is a demon who is after me.</i>

00:17:52.800 --> 00:17:58.390
<i>So that I can walk these lands, I must hide
from the demon by disguising myself like this.</i>

00:17:58.930 --> 00:18:03.930
Are you telling me that you've adopted
braids and glasses because of Hose?

00:18:03.930 --> 00:18:06.310
That isn't all of it, but yes.

00:18:06.560 --> 00:18:09.270
I think he's a really nice guy.

00:18:09.270 --> 00:18:11.070
I think so, too.

00:18:11.070 --> 00:18:13.820
He's definitely a kind and good person.

00:18:13.980 --> 00:18:15.280
Then, why...

00:18:15.860 --> 00:18:20.200
I was very popular in middle school.

00:18:21.030 --> 00:18:26.540
So there were a lot of people around me
who had nasty thoughts and ulterior motives.

00:18:27.120 --> 00:18:31.250
Boys and girls who wanted
to get chummy with the boys, too.

00:18:31.920 --> 00:18:36.550
The only one who wasn't indifferent
to my plight, who helped me, was Hazuki.

00:18:37.550 --> 00:18:41.930
Eventually, thanks to him,
only Hazuki and his friends were around me.

00:18:43.100 --> 00:18:44.430
But I...

00:18:45.060 --> 00:18:47.560
didn't want to be with Hazuki, either.

00:18:48.060 --> 00:18:51.900
It's because he has one major defect.

00:18:52.150 --> 00:18:53.860
Hose has a defect?

00:18:54.650 --> 00:18:58.320
Hazuki doesn't understand
the other side of people's feelings.

00:18:58.740 --> 00:19:00.660
The other side?

00:19:00.660 --> 00:19:04.790
Hazuki's good intentions
unintentionally harm people.

00:19:05.290 --> 00:19:07.000
Girls, especially.

00:19:07.540 --> 00:19:09.830
<i>S-So that's what it is.</i>

00:19:10.170 --> 00:19:12.500
<i>That's what felt out of place.</i>

00:19:12.500 --> 00:19:18.050
<i>For Hose, everything works out conveniently.</i>

00:19:18.670 --> 00:19:23.300
<i>The feelings of others
are stifled by his righteousness.</i>

00:19:24.470 --> 00:19:28.890
I know he's helped me
and that he's in the right.

00:19:29.810 --> 00:19:36.400
But I don't like it.
I don't want to be with him. And yet...

00:19:37.150 --> 00:19:41.200
<i>I see. She was trapped in a world
she never wished for.</i>

00:19:41.530 --> 00:19:46.740
He had special feelings for me. He fell in love.

00:19:47.120 --> 00:19:50.210
<i>She was chosen to be his "main heroine."</i>

00:19:50.540 --> 00:19:52.000
I couldn't forgive them.

00:19:52.920 --> 00:19:58.260
The girls who lied to themselves
about their feelings for Hazuki's sake, and...

00:19:58.800 --> 00:20:04.930
Hazuki himself, who had no awareness
of what he was doing to those girls. I couldn't...

00:20:04.930 --> 00:20:09.100
Is this what you were referring to before
with Tampopo?

00:20:09.430 --> 00:20:16.770
Yes. In middle school, the girls who were in love
with Hazuki would say things to me,

00:20:16.770 --> 00:20:19.820
and tried to push me
into becoming his girlfriend.

00:20:19.820 --> 00:20:21.900
So what happened?

00:20:21.900 --> 00:20:23.070
I refused.

00:20:23.570 --> 00:20:24.490
But...

00:20:25.410 --> 00:20:27.870
even so, he stayed by my side.

00:20:28.490 --> 00:20:32.500
To protect me, he resisted his own feelings.

00:20:34.830 --> 00:20:38.210
<i>If you really want to protect
the person who means a lot to you,</i>

00:20:38.210 --> 00:20:40.550
<i>you can't think about yourself getting hurt.</i>

00:20:41.090 --> 00:20:44.760
<i>The thing you should focus on the most
is that person, right?</i>

00:20:45.050 --> 00:20:48.890
<i>So that's what he was really talking about then?</i>

00:20:49.890 --> 00:20:53.940
I hate Hazuki for hurting people
with his kindness.

00:20:54.690 --> 00:20:56.810
But I can't say that.

00:20:57.520 --> 00:20:59.070
Because he helped me.

00:21:00.110 --> 00:21:02.700
Because I'm grateful to him for so much.

00:21:02.860 --> 00:21:04.820
Our eyes met.

00:21:04.820 --> 00:21:05.910
Really?

00:21:07.240 --> 00:21:12.540
Just to make sure,
you don't want to be around Hose, right?

00:21:16.710 --> 00:21:17.670
Got it.

00:21:18.340 --> 00:21:22.840
Then, I'll do something about it.
You don't have to worry.

00:21:25.130 --> 00:21:28.760
M-Me, too. I'll try to do my best
in my own way.

00:21:29.760 --> 00:21:32.680
I can't let you do all the work, Joro.

00:21:33.310 --> 00:21:35.850
Right. I'm counting on you.

00:21:36.230 --> 00:21:37.150
Good.

00:21:38.980 --> 00:21:40.400
Hey, Pansy.

00:21:40.770 --> 00:21:45.400
It's true what they say, the road to hell
is paved with good intentions.

00:23:16.410 --> 00:23:19.870
Sorry, asking you to meet me this late.

00:23:20.120 --> 00:23:21.330
It's okay.

00:23:21.960 --> 00:23:24.130
So, what did you want to tell me?

00:23:24.380 --> 00:23:28.130
Well, nothing really important...

00:23:29.260 --> 00:23:33.140
but I thought that my chance
has finally come around.

00:23:34.890 --> 00:23:39.890
EPISODE 12
THE ONE I LOVE IS...

00:23:36.310 --> 00:23:37.980
The One I Love is...
